BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (HFS Plus arrived with Mac OS 8.1 in 1998 as Mac OS Extended. Apple retained the familiar) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (Macintosh catalog, extent and fork concepts while replacing limitations of original HFS.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (Apple's TN1150 describes smaller average allocation-block waste on larger drives as a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (central motivation and specifies differences in filenames and metadata representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (During Mac OS X's lifetime, HFS Plus acquired optional journalling, hard-link handling,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (extensive permissions/attributes and the case-sensitive HFSX variant. APFS later replaced) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (it as the preferred modern Apple filesystem on many devices. HFS Plus and HFSX must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (identified as distinct modes and not treated as identical to original HFS.) Tj ET
