BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (The HFS Plus Volume Header is located 1024 bytes from the start of the volume. The format) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (organises its special metadata as files: allocation, catalog, extents overflow, attributes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (and startup files, alongside user file forks. The catalog, extents and attributes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (structures use B-trees with node sizes and key formats specified by the format.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (HFS Plus identifies allocation blocks with 32-bit numbers, permitting many more allocation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (units than original HFS. Multi-byte fields are big-endian. File and folder identifiers are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (CNIDs. Fork data descriptors include logical size, clump size, allocated blocks and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (extents, while overflow records extend the on-inode extent capacity.) Tj ET
