BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (dual-fork and Finder conventions. Its Unicode rules are historically specific and can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (differ from modern Unicode normalization. Integer timestamps use a 1904 epoch and have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (representational limits; time conversion must not assume Unix epochs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (It is a mutable B-tree format, not intrinsically copy-on-write. The case-sensitive HFSX) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (variant and optional journal require explicit detection. APFS snapshots, encryption) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (domains and object maps cannot be projected backward onto HFS Plus merely because both are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (Apple-designed.) Tj ET
